IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp2-seat`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part I, Divisions C to E -- CASES FOR THE SEAT LAYER (cp2-seat.l4).
--
-- At least one case for each of the seat's questions, with the facts a person in the seat would state. Every expected value
-- was decided by reading the section and written down before the run; none was copied from the output of a rule. A question
-- the Act does not answer is asserted as an explicit "not covered" value (NOTHING, or the layer-1 constructor that says the
-- text does not say), never as FALSE or 0. One assertion to a line. Money is in dollars, a rate is asked in per cent
-- (5 means 5%), and a date is written YMD year month day.


§ `If you are an employee: CPP deductions from your pay (ss 21 to 21.01, 26)`

-- Must my employer deduct CPP contributions from my pay (s 21(1))
-- An ordinary employee in pensionable employment who is being paid: the duty arises (s 21(1)).
#ASSERT `Must my employer deduct CPP contributions from my pay (s 21(1))` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Employment that is not pensionable: no duty.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my employer deduct CPP contributions from my pay (s 21(1))` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- No remuneration is being paid: no duty.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my employer deduct CPP contributions from my pay (s 21(1))` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- An officer is an employee, and the person who pays the officer is the employer (s 2(1)).
#ASSERT `Must my employer deduct CPP contributions from my pay (s 21(1))` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE

-- How much must my employer deduct from this payment of pay (s 21(1))
-- The amount the prescribed rules give is the amount to deduct.
#ASSERT `How much must my employer deduct from this payment of pay (s 21(1))` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 118.45 EQUALS 118.45
-- Not pensionable: nothing is deducted.
#ASSERT `How much must my employer deduct from this payment of pay (s 21(1))` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 118.45 EQUALS 0

-- Am I treated as having told the Minister that my employer did not deduct a CPP contribution from my pay (s 21(3.1))
-- Ruling that no deduction was needed, not based on incorrect information, later decided it should have been made, employer paid: deemed notified (s 21(3.1)).
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having told the Minister that my employer did not deduct a CPP contribution from my pay (s 21(3.1))` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- The ruling rested on incorrect information, so the employer is not relieved under (3): not deemed notified.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as having told the Minister that my employer did not deduct a CPP contribution from my pay (s 21(3.1))` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Nothing paid yet: not deemed notified.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as having told the Minister that my employer did not deduct a CPP contribution from my pay (s 21(3.1))` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- Can my employer take a CPP deduction it missed from a later payment of my pay (s 21(4))
-- Within 12 months, one missed amount (s 21(4)).
#ASSERT `Can my employer take a CPP deduction it missed from a later payment of my pay (s 21(4))` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 9 15) 1
-- One day after the 12 months.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my employer take a CPP deduction it missed from a later payment of my pay (s 21(4))` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2027 1 16) 1)
-- More than one earlier missed amount.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my employer take a CPP deduction it missed from a later payment of my pay (s 21(4))` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 9 15) 2)
-- No amount was missed.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my employer take a CPP deduction it missed from a later payment of my pay (s 21(4))` FALSE (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 9 15) 1)

-- Am I treated as having received the amount that was deducted from my pay (s 21(5))
-- Deducted: deemed received (s 21(5)).
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having received the amount that was deducted from my pay (s 21(5))` TRUE
-- Nothing deducted.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as having received the amount that was deducted from my pay (s 21(5))` FALSE)

-- On what day am I treated as having received the amount that was deducted from my pay (s 21(5))
-- Treated as received at the time it was deducted (s 21(5)).
#ASSERT `On what day am I treated as having received the amount that was deducted from my pay (s 21(5))` (YMD 2026 5 29) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 29

-- Is the CPP deduction taken from a pay overpayment treated as never deducted (s 21.01(1))
-- Election and repayment before the end of 2027, no correcting return, conditions met (s 21.01(1)).
#ASSERT `Is the CPP deduction taken from a pay overpayment treated as never deducted (s 21.01(1))` 2024 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 7 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE
-- Election in 2028 is after the end of the third year after 2024.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the CPP deduction taken from a pay overpayment treated as never deducted (s 21.01(1))` 2024 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2028 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 7 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE)
-- The rule is for years after 2015.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the CPP deduction taken from a pay overpayment treated as never deducted (s 21.01(1))` 2015 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2016 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2016 7 1) FALSE (YMD 2016 1 1) TRUE)
-- Not an excess payment made by mistake.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the CPP deduction taken from a pay overpayment treated as never deducted (s 21.01(1))` 2024 FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 7 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE)

-- How much of the CPP deduction is treated as never deducted (s 21.01(2))
-- The lesser of the amount deducted and A minus B (s 21.01(2)).
#ASSERT `How much of the CPP deduction is treated as never deducted (s 21.01(2))` 500 3000 2800 EQUALS 200
-- A minus B is larger than the amount deducted.
#ASSERT `How much of the CPP deduction is treated as never deducted (s 21.01(2))` 500 3000 2000 EQUALS 500

-- Does section 26(1) protect my employer from an action by me for deducting CPP contributions from my pay (s 26(1))
-- A deduction made in compliance or intended compliance: no action lies (s 26(1)).
#ASSERT `Does section 26(1) protect my employer from an action by me for deducting CPP contributions from my pay (s 26(1))` TRUE TRUE
-- Not in compliance or intended compliance: the section does not protect.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 26(1) protect my employer from an action by me for deducting CPP contributions from my pay (s 26(1))` TRUE FALSE)
-- Nothing was deducted.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 26(1) protect my employer from an action by me for deducting CPP contributions from my pay (s 26(1))` FALSE TRUE)

-- To what extent does the Minister's receipt discharge what my employer owes me (s 26(2))
-- Receipt for 300, owed 300 (s 26(2)).
#ASSERT `To what extent does the Minister's receipt discharge what my employer owes me (s 26(2))` TRUE 300 300 EQUALS 300
-- Discharge only to the extent of the receipt.
#ASSERT `To what extent does the Minister's receipt discharge what my employer owes me (s 26(2))` TRUE 200 300 EQUALS 200
-- Never more than what is owed.
#ASSERT `To what extent does the Minister's receipt discharge what my employer owes me (s 26(2))` TRUE 300 200 EQUALS 200
-- No receipt: no discharge.
#ASSERT `To what extent does the Minister's receipt discharge what my employer owes me (s 26(2))` FALSE 300 300 EQUALS 0


§ `If you employ people, are a company director, or administer someone else's affairs (ss 21 to 24, 27.1, 38, 41)`

-- Must I, as an employer, deduct CPP contributions from what I pay an employee (s 21(1))
-- The employer's own duty to deduct (s 21(1)).
#ASSERT `Must I, as an employer, deduct CPP contributions from what I pay an employee (s 21(1))` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Not pensionable employment.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I, as an employer, deduct CPP contributions from what I pay an employee (s 21(1))` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- An officer who receives remuneration from me: I am the employer (s 2(1)); the officer is an employee.
#ASSERT `Must I, as an employer, deduct CPP contributions from what I pay an employee (s 21(1))` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- I am not liable to pay the worker and the worker holds no office: I am not the employer.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I, as an employer, deduct CPP contributions from what I pay an employee (s 21(1))` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- How much must I remit to the Receiver General for an employee, including my own contribution (s 21(1))
-- Employee's deduction plus the employer's own amount (s 21(1)).
#ASSERT `How much must I remit to the Receiver General for an employee, including my own contribution (s 21(1))` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 118.45 118.45 EQUALS 236.9
-- Not pensionable: nothing to remit.
#ASSERT `How much must I remit to the Receiver General for an employee, including my own contribution (s 21(1))` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE 118.45 118.45 EQUALS 0

-- Where must I remit the amounts I deduct (s 21(1))
-- A prescribed person remits to the account at a financial institution (s 21(1)).
#ASSERT `Where must I remit the amounts I deduct (s 21(1))` TRUE EQUALS `the amount is remitted to the account of the Receiver General at a financial institution`
-- Anyone else remits to the Receiver General.
#ASSERT `Where must I remit the amounts I deduct (s 21(1))` FALSE EQUALS `the amount is remitted to the Receiver General`

-- If I am a prescribed person, am I treated as having remitted to the account at a financial institution (s 21(1.1))
-- Remitted a day before the due day (s 21(1.1)).
#ASSERT `If I am a prescribed person, am I treated as having remitted to the account at a financial institution (s 21(1.1))` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 14) (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- Remitted on the due day itself: not at least one day before.
#ASSERT NOT (`If I am a prescribed person, am I treated as having remitted to the account at a financial institution (s 21(1.1))` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 15))
-- Not a prescribed person.
#ASSERT NOT (`If I am a prescribed person, am I treated as having remitted to the account at a financial institution (s 21(1.1))` FALSE (YMD 2026 1 14) (YMD 2026 1 15))

-- Was my remittance made in the manner the Act requires (s 21(1))
-- Not a prescribed person: any remittance to the Receiver General is in the manner required.
#ASSERT `Was my remittance made in the manner the Act requires (s 21(1))` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- A prescribed person who remitted to the Receiver General on the due day, not to the account.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my remittance made in the manner the Act requires (s 21(1))` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 15))
-- Remitted a day early: deemed to the account (s 21(1.1)).
#ASSERT `Was my remittance made in the manner the Act requires (s 21(1))` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 14) (YMD 2026 1 15)

-- Am I relieved of liability for an amount I failed to deduct because of a ruling (s 21(3))
-- All three limbs of s 21(3).
#ASSERT `Am I relieved of liability for an amount I failed to deduct because of a ruling (s 21(3))` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- The ruling was based on incorrect information.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I relieved of liability for an amount I failed to deduct because of a ruling (s 21(3))` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- It was not later decided that the deduction should have been made.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I relieved of liability for an amount I failed to deduct because of a ruling (s 21(3))` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- Am I liable to pay Her Majesty the whole amount I failed to deduct and remit (s 21(2))
-- Failed to deduct and remit, no ruling relief (s 21(2)).
#ASSERT `Am I liable to pay Her Majesty the whole amount I failed to deduct and remit (s 21(2))` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Relieved by s 21(3): not liable.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I liable to pay Her Majesty the whole amount I failed to deduct and remit (s 21(2))` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- No failure.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I liable to pay Her Majesty the whole amount I failed to deduct and remit (s 21(2))` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- How much must I pay Her Majesty for the amount I failed to deduct and remit (s 21(2))
-- The whole amount that should have been deducted and remitted (s 21(2)).
#ASSERT `How much must I pay Her Majesty for the amount I failed to deduct and remit (s 21(2))` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 800 EQUALS 800
-- Relieved by s 21(3).
#ASSERT `How much must I pay Her Majesty for the amount I failed to deduct and remit (s 21(2))` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 800 EQUALS 0

-- From what time am I liable to pay the amount I failed to deduct (s 21(2))
-- From the time it should have been deducted (s 21(2)).
#ASSERT `From what time am I liable to pay the amount I failed to deduct (s 21(2))` (YMD 2026 3 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31

-- After a decision that I should have deducted, do I owe my own contribution without interest or penalties (s 21(3.1))
-- Relieved by (3), decision communicated: liable without interest or penalties (s 21(3.1)).
#ASSERT `After a decision that I should have deducted, do I owe my own contribution without interest or penalties (s 21(3.1))` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Decision not yet communicated.
#ASSERT NOT (`After a decision that I should have deducted, do I owe my own contribution without interest or penalties (s 21(3.1))` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- No ruling: the (3.1) route does not arise.
#ASSERT NOT (`After a decision that I should have deducted, do I owe my own contribution without interest or penalties (s 21(3.1))` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- How much of my own contribution do I owe after that decision, without interest or penalties (s 21(3.1))
-- Relieved by (3), decision communicated: the employer's contribution, without interest or penalties (s 21(3.1)).
#ASSERT `How much of my own contribution do I owe after that decision, without interest or penalties (s 21(3.1))` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 300 EQUALS 300
-- Decision not yet communicated.
#ASSERT `How much of my own contribution do I owe after that decision, without interest or penalties (s 21(3.1))` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 300 EQUALS 0

-- How much interest must I pay on an amount I did not remit when required (s 21(6))
-- 10,000 at 5 per cent for 73 days over 365 is 100 (s 21(6)).
#ASSERT `How much interest must I pay on an amount I did not remit when required (s 21(6))` 10000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 3 15) 5 EQUALS 100
-- Remitted before it was required: no interest.
#ASSERT `How much interest must I pay on an amount I did not remit when required (s 21(6))` 10000 (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 1) 5 EQUALS 0

-- Did I fail to remit the amount at the time required (s 21(7))
-- Never received (s 21(7)).
#ASSERT `Did I fail to remit the amount at the time required (s 21(7))` (YMD 2026 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 15) TRUE
-- Received on the due day in the manner required.
#ASSERT NOT (`Did I fail to remit the amount at the time required (s 21(7))` (YMD 2026 1 15) TRUE (YMD 2026 1 15) TRUE)
-- Received a day late.
#ASSERT `Did I fail to remit the amount at the time required (s 21(7))` (YMD 2026 1 15) TRUE (YMD 2026 1 16) TRUE

-- What percentage penalty applies to an amount I did not remit when required (s 21(7))
-- Four days late: 5 per cent (s 21(7)(a)(ii)(B)).
#ASSERT `What percentage penalty applies to an amount I did not remit when required (s 21(7))` (YMD 2026 1 15) TRUE (YMD 2026 1 19) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 5%
-- Never received: 10 per cent (s 21(7)(a)(iii)).
#ASSERT `What percentage penalty applies to an amount I did not remit when required (s 21(7))` (YMD 2026 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 15) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 10%
-- A repeat, knowing or grossly negligent failure: 20 per cent (s 21(7)(b)).
#ASSERT `What percentage penalty applies to an amount I did not remit when required (s 21(7))` (YMD 2026 1 15) TRUE (YMD 2026 1 16) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS 20%
-- Received on the due day in the manner required: no penalty.
#ASSERT `What percentage penalty applies to an amount I did not remit when required (s 21(7))` (YMD 2026 1 15) TRUE (YMD 2026 1 15) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0

-- How much is the penalty for an amount I did not remit when required (s 21(7))
-- Five days late: 5 per cent of 10,000 (s 21(7)).
#ASSERT `How much is the penalty for an amount I did not remit when required (s 21(7))` 10000 (YMD 2026 1 15) TRUE (YMD 2026 1 20) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 500

-- Am I, as a director, jointly and severally liable with the corporation for CPP it failed to deduct or remit (s 21.1(1))
-- A director of a corporate employer when the failure occurred (s 21.1(1)).
#ASSERT `Am I, as a director, jointly and severally liable with the corporation for CPP it failed to deduct or remit (s 21.1(1))` TRUE TRUE
-- Not a director then.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I, as a director, jointly and severally liable with the corporation for CPP it failed to deduct or remit (s 21.1(1))` TRUE FALSE)
-- The employer is not a corporation.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I, as a director, jointly and severally liable with the corporation for CPP it failed to deduct or remit (s 21.1(1))` FALSE TRUE)

-- How much am I liable for as a director, with interest and penalties (s 21.1(1))
-- The amount, with the interest and penalties relating to it.
#ASSERT `How much am I liable for as a director, with interest and penalties (s 21.1(1))` TRUE TRUE 1000 50 100 EQUALS 1150
-- Not a corporate employer.
#ASSERT `How much am I liable for as a director, with interest and penalties (s 21.1(1))` FALSE TRUE 1000 50 100 EQUALS 0

-- Am I, as a director, still liable after the Income Tax Act limits and defences apply (s 21.1(2))
-- Liable and no limit or defence relieves the director (s 21.1(2)).
#ASSERT `Am I, as a director, still liable after the Income Tax Act limits and defences apply (s 21.1(2))` TRUE FALSE
-- A limit or defence relieves the director.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I, as a director, still liable after the Income Tax Act limits and defences apply (s 21.1(2))` TRUE TRUE)

-- Do the assessment rules and an assessed employer's rights apply to me as a director (s 21.1(3))
-- They apply to the director (s 21.1(3)).
#ASSERT `Do the assessment rules and an assessed employer's rights apply to me as a director (s 21.1(3))` TRUE
-- Not liable under 21.1(1).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the assessment rules and an assessed employer's rights apply to me as a director (s 21.1(3))` FALSE)

-- May the Minister assess me as an employer for an amount I owe under the Act (s 22(1))
-- An amount is payable by the employer (s 22(1)).
#ASSERT `May the Minister assess me as an employer for an amount I owe under the Act (s 22(1))` TRUE
-- Nothing is payable.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Minister assess me as an employer for an amount I owe under the Act (s 22(1))` FALSE)

-- Must I pay the amount of the assessment at once (s 22(2))
-- Notice sent, not vacated (s 22(2)).
#ASSERT `Must I pay the amount of the assessment at once (s 22(2))` TRUE FALSE
-- Vacated on appeal.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I pay the amount of the assessment at once (s 22(2))` TRUE TRUE)

-- How much must I pay at once on the assessment (s 22(2))
-- The assessed amount forthwith (s 22(2)).
#ASSERT `How much must I pay at once on the assessment (s 22(2))` TRUE FALSE 4200 EQUALS 4200
-- Vacated on appeal.
#ASSERT `How much must I pay at once on the assessment (s 22(2))` TRUE TRUE 4200 EQUALS 0

-- Is it too late for the Minister to assess me as an employer (s 22(3))
-- One day after four years from the earliest due day (s 22(3)).
#ASSERT `Is it too late for the Minister to assess me as an employer (s 22(3))` (YMD 2024 1 16) (YMD 2020 1 15) FALSE
-- On the last day of the four years: still in time.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is it too late for the Minister to assess me as an employer (s 22(3))` (YMD 2024 1 15) (YMD 2020 1 15) FALSE)
-- Misrepresentation or fraud: no limit.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is it too late for the Minister to assess me as an employer (s 22(3))` (YMD 2031 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 15) TRUE)

-- Can I appeal my assessment to the Minister for reconsideration (s 27.1)
-- Day 90 after being notified (s 27.1).
#ASSERT `Can I appeal my assessment to the Minister for reconsideration (s 27.1)` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 4 1)
-- Day 91.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I appeal my assessment to the Minister for reconsideration (s 27.1)` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 4 2))

-- What is the last day I can appeal my assessment to the Minister (s 27.1)
-- 90 days after 1 January 2026 (s 27.1).
#ASSERT `What is the last day I can appeal my assessment to the Minister (s 27.1)` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 1

-- Is a CPP amount I owe a debt to Her Majesty that can be recovered in court (s 23(1))
-- A debt due to Her Majesty, recoverable in the Federal Court (s 23(1)).
#ASSERT `Is a CPP amount I owe a debt to Her Majesty that can be recovered in court (s 23(1))` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Neither that court nor a manner the Act provides.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a CPP amount I owe a debt to Her Majesty that can be recovered in court (s 23(1))` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- Do the listed Income Tax Act collection provisions apply to a CPP amount I owe (s 23(2))
-- They apply to an amount payable under the Act (s 23(2)).
#ASSERT `Do the listed Income Tax Act collection provisions apply to a CPP amount I owe (s 23(2))` TRUE
-- Not an amount payable under the Act.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the listed Income Tax Act collection provisions apply to a CPP amount I owe (s 23(2))` FALSE)

-- Does subsection 224(1.2) of the Income Tax Act apply to the contributions and related amounts I owe (s 23(2)(b))
-- Employer's or employee's contributions, no stay (s 23(2)(b)).
#ASSERT `Does subsection 224(1.2) of the Income Tax Act apply to the contributions and related amounts I owe (s 23(2)(b))` TRUE FALSE
-- Subject to the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act stay.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does subsection 224(1.2) of the Income Tax Act apply to the contributions and related amounts I owe (s 23(2)(b))` TRUE TRUE)

-- Do I hold the CPP I deducted from my employee's pay in trust for Her Majesty (s 23(3))
-- Deducted and not remitted: held in trust (s 23(3)).
#ASSERT `Do I hold the CPP I deducted from my employee's pay in trust for Her Majesty (s 23(3))` TRUE FALSE
-- Remitted: no trust.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I hold the CPP I deducted from my employee's pay in trust for Her Majesty (s 23(3))` TRUE TRUE)

-- How much do I hold in trust for Her Majesty (s 23(3))
-- Deducted 900, remitted 400 (s 23(3)).
#ASSERT `How much do I hold in trust for Her Majesty (s 23(3))` 900 400 EQUALS 500
-- All remitted.
#ASSERT `How much do I hold in trust for Her Majesty (s 23(3))` 900 900 EQUALS 0

-- Is an interest a security interest for the trust rules, or is it a prescribed one (s 23(4.1))
-- A security interest that is not prescribed (s 23(4.1)).
#ASSERT `Is an interest a security interest for the trust rules, or is it a prescribed one (s 23(4.1))` TRUE FALSE
-- A prescribed security interest is not one for (3) and (4).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is an interest a security interest for the trust rules, or is it a prescribed one (s 23(4.1))` TRUE TRUE)

-- What is the value of my property that is deemed held in trust for Her Majesty (s 23(4))
-- Unpaid: property equal in value to the trust amount (s 23(4)).
#ASSERT `What is the value of my property that is deemed held in trust for Her Majesty (s 23(4))` 500 FALSE EQUALS 500
-- Paid to Her Majesty in time.
#ASSERT `What is the value of my property that is deemed held in trust for Her Majesty (s 23(4))` 500 TRUE EQUALS 0

-- From what time is my property deemed to be held in trust for Her Majesty (s 23(4)(a))
-- From the time the amount was deducted (s 23(4)(a)).
#ASSERT `From what time is my property deemed to be held in trust for Her Majesty (s 23(4)(a))` (YMD 2026 2 27) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 27

-- Does Her Majesty's claim to my property rank ahead of a security interest in it (s 23(4))
-- Her Majesty ranks ahead (s 23(4)).
#ASSERT `Does Her Majesty's claim to my property rank ahead of a security interest in it (s 23(4))` 500 TRUE FALSE
-- Sections 81.1 or 81.2 of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act give the other claimant priority.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does Her Majesty's claim to my property rank ahead of a security interest in it (s 23(4))` 500 TRUE TRUE)
-- No trust property.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does Her Majesty's claim to my property rank ahead of a security interest in it (s 23(4))` 0 TRUE FALSE)

-- Am I a responsible representative under section 23 (s 23(5))
-- An executor winding up an estate (s 23(5)).
#ASSERT `Am I a responsible representative under section 23 (s 23(5))` `an executor dealing with another person's estate` TRUE
-- A trustee in bankruptcy is excluded.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a responsible representative under section 23 (s 23(5))` `a trustee in bankruptcy dealing with another person's property` TRUE)
-- None of the listed kinds.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a responsible representative under section 23 (s 23(5))` `a person of no such kind` TRUE)

-- Must I obtain a certificate from the Minister before I distribute property I administer (s 23(5))
-- Before distributing property (s 23(5)).
#ASSERT `Must I obtain a certificate from the Minister before I distribute property I administer (s 23(5))` `an executor dealing with another person's estate` TRUE TRUE
-- Not about to distribute.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I obtain a certificate from the Minister before I distribute property I administer (s 23(5))` `an executor dealing with another person's estate` TRUE FALSE)

-- May the Minister certify that the amounts I must have covered are paid or secured (s 23(5))
-- Both sets of amounts paid (s 23(5)).
#ASSERT `May the Minister certify that the amounts I must have covered are paid or secured (s 23(5))` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Security accepted.
#ASSERT `May the Minister certify that the amounts I must have covered are paid or secured (s 23(5))` FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Only the employer's amounts are paid.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Minister certify that the amounts I must have covered are paid or secured (s 23(5))` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- Am I personally liable if I distributed property without a certificate (s 23(5.1))
-- Distributed without a certificate (s 23(5.1)).
#ASSERT `Am I personally liable if I distributed property without a certificate (s 23(5.1))` `an executor dealing with another person's estate` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- A certificate was obtained.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I personally liable if I distributed property without a certificate (s 23(5.1))` `an executor dealing with another person's estate` TRUE TRUE TRUE)

-- How much am I personally liable for if I distributed property without a certificate (s 23(5.1))
-- To the extent of the value of the property distributed (s 23(5.1)).
#ASSERT `How much am I personally liable for if I distributed property without a certificate (s 23(5.1))` `an executor dealing with another person's estate` TRUE TRUE FALSE 10000 6000 EQUALS 6000
-- Never more than the amounts.
#ASSERT `How much am I personally liable for if I distributed property without a certificate (s 23(5.1))` `an executor dealing with another person's estate` TRUE TRUE FALSE 10000 25000 EQUALS 10000
-- A certificate was obtained.
#ASSERT `How much am I personally liable for if I distributed property without a certificate (s 23(5.1))` `an executor dealing with another person's estate` TRUE TRUE TRUE 10000 6000 EQUALS 0

-- Am I the bankrupt employer's agent for all purposes of the Act (s 23(6))
-- The trustee is deemed the agent of the bankrupt (s 23(6)).
#ASSERT `Am I the bankrupt employer's agent for all purposes of the Act (s 23(6))` TRUE TRUE
-- Not the trustee.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I the bankrupt employer's agent for all purposes of the Act (s 23(6))` TRUE FALSE)

-- Must I, as an employer, keep records and books of account (s 24(1))
-- Pays remuneration to an employee in pensionable employment (s 24(1)).
#ASSERT `Must I, as an employer, keep records and books of account (s 24(1))` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Not pensionable employment.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I, as an employer, keep records and books of account (s 24(1))` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)

-- May I keep my records and books of account at a given place (s 24(1))
-- Residence in Canada is allowed (s 24(1)).
